Data handling
-------------
This tool reads an Apple Intelligence Report JSON export and writes CSV,
HTML, TXT, Markdown, and JSON files derived from it. That data includes your
prompts and the model's responses in plain text, unless you pass --redact.

Zero network calls
-------------------
This tool makes no network requests of any kind, at any point in its
execution. It is a single Python 3 file using only the Python standard
library. It reads exactly one file (the report you point it at) and writes
to exactly one directory (the one you specify). There are no telemetry
calls, no update checks, no analytics, and no third-party services
involved.

No subprocess, no dynamic execution
------------------------------------
This tool does not invoke subprocess, os.system, eval(), exec(), or any
other mechanism to run external commands or dynamically execute code.

Local processing only
----------------------
All parsing happens locally, in-process, on the machine you run it on.
Nothing is uploaded, synced, or transmitted anywhere by this tool.

Your responsibility
--------------------
Once this tool writes output files, those files are as sensitive as your
original report: they may contain the full text of prompts you sent to
Apple Intelligence and the responses you received. The authors are not
responsible for what you do with parsed output after it is written.
This includes, but is not limited to, committing it to a repository,
uploading it to a cloud sync folder, pasting it into a chat, or sharing it
with a third party. Use --redact if you need to share the shape of your
usage (timestamps, apps, origin, counts) without exposing the content.

